Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:42:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(trpc): validate credential keys per app on the server

updateAppCredentials used to merge whatever the client sent into
credential.key; only the Setup screens validated the fields. Now:
- btcpayserver, alby and hitpay are checked against their own schemas
  from the app-store (loaded on demand, like PayPal's validator): a
  missing field or a wrong type is a BAD_REQUEST and nothing is written,
  and fields outside the schema are dropped;
- apps without a server-side validator, and credentials without an
  appId, get a BAD_REQUEST instead of having their key overwritten
  (keys stored as encrypted strings were being spread into characters);
- a stored key that is not an object is no longer spread.

The seven characterization tests that documented the defect are
inverted; the other seven pass unchanged. A guard test checks that
every Setup screen calling this route has a validator registered.

Refs #30566
